Formally, the activation of the $i$-th neuron in the hidden layer is given by
\begin{equation}
a_{i}^{(1)}=ReLU\left(\sum_{j=1}^r w_{ji}^{(1)}x_{j}+b_{i}^{(1)}\right),~i=1,2,\dots,20,
\label{eqn:hidden}
\end{equation}
where $r$ is the number of neurons of the input layer, $x_{j}$ is the $j$-th feature (normalized, see Section~\ref{sec:model}), and $w_{ji}^{(1)}$ and $b_{i}^{(1)}$ are weights and biases of the $i$-th neuron in the hidden layer, respectively.
The activation of the output neuron is given by
\begin{equation}
a^{(2)}=\sigma\left(\sum_{i=1}^{20} w_{i}^{(2)}a_{i}^{(1)}+b^{(2)}\right),\\
\end{equation}
where $w_{i}^{(2)}$ and $b^{(2)}$ are weights and the bias of the output neuron, respectively. In these two equations,
\begin{equation*}
ReLU(x)=\begin{cases}x, & \text{if } x > 0,\\0, & \text{otherwise}\end{cases},~\sigma(x)=\frac{1}{1+e^{-x}}
\end{equation*}
are ReLU and sigmoid functions, respectively.

